"use strict";(self.webpackChunkdatabricks_monolith=self.webpackChunkdatabricks_monolith||[]).push([[11157],{11157:e=>{e.exports="# Query Metric Views\n\nThis skill provides guidance for querying metric views in Databricks.\n\n## What are Metric Views?\n\nMetric views are special table-like assets designed to support business intelligence queries. They differ from regular tables in their structure and querying requirements.\n\n### Components\n\nMetric views contain two types of columns:\n\n1. **Dimensions**: Behave like normal table columns (e.g., `store_type`, `state`, `cloud`, `order_date`)\n   - Can be selected, transformed, filtered, and grouped like regular columns\n   - Used in SELECT, WHERE, GROUP BY, and HAVING clauses\n\n2. **Measures**: Special columns representing pre-aggregated metrics (e.g., `revenue`, `customer_count`, `active_users`)\n   - The aggregation logic is built into the measure definition\n   - MUST be wrapped in `MEASURE()` function when queried\n   - Cannot be selected without aggregation\n   - Only make sense when aggregated over multiple rows\n\n## Querying Rules\n\nWhen querying metric views, follow these critical rules:\n\n### Core Constraints\n\n1. **Measure wrapping**: Every measure must use the `MEASURE()` function\n\n   ```sql\n   -- CORRECT\n   SELECT MEASURE(`revenue`) AS `revenue`\n\n   -- INCORRECT\n   SELECT `revenue`\n   ```\n\n2. **Backtick escaping**: All dimensions and measures in expressions MUST be escaped with backticks\n\n   ```sql\n   MEASURE(`revenue`)\n   `Order Date` >= '2024-01-01'\n   `cloud` = 'AWS'\n   ```\n\n3. **GROUP BY ALL required**: When selecting measures, you must include `GROUP BY ALL`\n\n   ```sql\n   SELECT `cloud`, MEASURE(`revenue`) AS `revenue`\n   FROM catalog.schema.metric_view\n   GROUP BY ALL\n   ```\n\n4. **No nested aggregations**: Cannot wrap measures in other aggregation functions\n\n   ```sql\n   -- INCORRECT\n   MEASURE(AVG(`revenue`))\n   AVG(MEASURE(`revenue`))\n   MAX(MEASURE(`revenue`))\n\n   -- CORRECT: Use ORDER BY + LIMIT for min/max\n   SELECT `cloud`, MEASURE(`revenue`) AS `revenue`\n   FROM catalog.schema.metric_view\n   GROUP BY ALL\n   ORDER BY `revenue` DESC\n   LIMIT 1\n   ```\n\n5. **No AVG on measures**: Calculate average by dividing measures\n\n   ```sql\n   -- INCORRECT\n   AVG(MEASURE(`revenue`))\n\n   -- CORRECT\n   MEASURE(`revenue`) / MEASURE(`count`) AS `average_revenue`\n   ```\n\n6. **No joins before aggregation**: Cannot join metric views with tables or other metric views before aggregating\n   - First aggregate the metric view in a CTE\n   - Then join the CTE with other tables\n\n7. **Arithmetic on measures**: Can only perform arithmetic on post-aggregated measures\n\n   ```sql\n   -- INCORRECT (pre-aggregation arithmetic)\n   MEASURE(`revenue` / `count`)\n\n   -- CORRECT (post-aggregation arithmetic)\n   MEASURE(`revenue`) / MEASURE(`count`)\n   ```\n\n### Dimensions\n\nDimensions can be treated like normal columns:\n\n- Can be used in WHERE clauses for filtering\n- Can be transformed with functions (e.g., `DATE_TRUNC('MONTH', \\`Order Date\\`)`)\n- Can be used in GROUP BY, ORDER BY, and HAVING clauses\n- Can be used with COUNT DISTINCT and other aggregations\n\n## Query Examples\n\n### Simple Aggregation\n\n```sql\n-- Revenue per cloud provider\nSELECT `cloud`, MEASURE(`revenue`) AS `revenue`\nFROM catalog.schema.sales_metric_view\nGROUP BY ALL\nORDER BY `revenue` DESC\n```\n\n### With Time-based Dimensions\n\n```sql\n-- Monthly customer count for 2024\nSELECT\n  DATE_TRUNC('MONTH', `Order Date`) AS `month`,\n  MEASURE(`customer_count`) AS `customer_count`\nFROM catalog.schema.sales_metric_view\nWHERE YEAR(`Order Date`) = 2024\nGROUP BY ALL\nORDER BY `month`\n```\n\n### Computed Measures\n\n```sql\n-- Total revenue (combining two measures)\nSELECT\n  `region`,\n  MEASURE(`direct_revenue`) + MEASURE(`indirect_revenue`) AS `total_revenue`\nFROM catalog.schema.sales_metric_view\nGROUP BY ALL\n```\n\n### Average Calculation\n\n```sql\n-- Average revenue per customer\nSELECT\n  MEASURE(`revenue`) / MEASURE(`customer_count`) AS `avg_revenue_per_customer`\nFROM catalog.schema.sales_metric_view\nGROUP BY ALL\n```\n\n### Filtering with HAVING\n\n```sql\n-- Clouds with revenue above threshold\nSELECT `cloud`, MEASURE(`revenue`) AS `revenue`\nFROM catalog.schema.sales_metric_view\nGROUP BY ALL\nHAVING `revenue` > 100000\nORDER BY `revenue` DESC\n```\n\n### Multiple Dimensions\n\n```sql\n-- Revenue per region and product, filtered by year\nSELECT\n  `region`,\n  `product_sku`,\n  MEASURE(`revenue`) AS `revenue`\nFROM catalog.schema.sales_metric_view\nWHERE YEAR(`Order Date`) = 2024\nGROUP BY ALL\nORDER BY `revenue` DESC\n```\n\n### Using CTEs for Top-K\n\n```sql\n-- Monthly revenue for top 3 products\nWITH top_products AS (\n  SELECT `product_sku`, MEASURE(`revenue`) AS `total_revenue`\n  FROM catalog.schema.sales_metric_view\n  WHERE YEAR(`Order Date`) = 2024\n  GROUP BY ALL\n  ORDER BY `total_revenue` DESC\n  LIMIT 3\n)\nSELECT\n  DATE_TRUNC('MONTH', `Order Date`) AS `month`,\n  `product_sku`,\n  MEASURE(`revenue`) AS `monthly_revenue`\nFROM catalog.schema.sales_metric_view\nWHERE YEAR(`Order Date`) = 2024\n  AND `product_sku` IN (SELECT `product_sku` FROM top_products)\nGROUP BY ALL\nORDER BY `month`, `product_sku`\n```\n\n### Window Functions\n\n```sql\n-- Month-over-month revenue change\nSELECT\n  DATE_TRUNC('MONTH', `Order Date`) AS `month`,\n  MEASURE(`revenue`) AS `monthly_revenue`,\n  MEASURE(`revenue`) - LAG(MEASURE(`revenue`)) OVER (ORDER BY DATE_TRUNC('MONTH', `Order Date`)) AS `revenue_change`\nFROM catalog.schema.sales_metric_view\nGROUP BY ALL\nORDER BY `month`\n```\n\n## Common Patterns\n\n### Getting Totals\n\nWhen no dimensions are selected, you get a single row with totals:\n\n```sql\nSELECT MEASURE(`revenue`) AS `total_revenue`\nFROM catalog.schema.sales_metric_view\nGROUP BY ALL\n```\n\n### Best/Worst Performers\n\nUse ORDER BY + LIMIT instead of MAX/MIN:\n\n```sql\n-- Worst performing region\nSELECT `region`, MEASURE(`revenue`) AS `revenue`\nFROM catalog.schema.sales_metric_view\nGROUP BY ALL\nORDER BY `revenue` ASC\nLIMIT 1\n```\n\n### Percentage Calculations\n\n```sql\n-- Revenue percentage by region\nWITH total AS (\n  SELECT MEASURE(`revenue`) AS `total_revenue`\n  FROM catalog.schema.sales_metric_view\n  GROUP BY ALL\n)\nSELECT\n  `region`,\n  MEASURE(`revenue`) AS `revenue`,\n  (MEASURE(`revenue`) / (SELECT `total_revenue` FROM total)) * 100 AS `revenue_percentage`\nFROM catalog.schema.sales_metric_view\nGROUP BY ALL\n```\n\n## When to Use This Skill\n\nUse this skill when:\n\n- You encounter table with `type: METRIC_VIEW`\n- You need to write queries involving `MEASURE()` function\n"}}]);
